WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:05.040
The new "Dungeons &amp; Dragons" movie is drawing&nbsp;
comparisons to an entirely different and very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:09.360
popular franchise. But is that a good thing&nbsp;
or a bad thing? Here's what fans are saying.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:13.680
Paramount Pictures has debuted a new trailer for&nbsp;
their upcoming fantasy epic "Dungeons &amp; Dragons:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:17.640
Honor Among Thieves," causing fans to&nbsp;
draw flattering comparisons to one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:20.220
the most beloved movies of the 2010s. The film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:23.820
which is adapted from the vast lore of the&nbsp;
tabletop role-playing game of the same name,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:28.560
boasts a stacked cast including Chris Pine,&nbsp;
Michelle Rodriguez, and Regé-Jean Page.

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:32.280
Despite this impressive roster, the&nbsp;
project faces an uphill battle. Though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:36.300
the "Dungeons &amp; Dragons" brand is as popular&nbsp;
as it's ever been thanks to its inclusion in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:40.680
shows like "Stranger Things," making a film or&nbsp;
television series as engaging and satisfying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:45.240
as an interactive game is a challenge. Plus,&nbsp;
past adaptations haven't quite hit the mark.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:55.200
Regardless, some fans have noted that&nbsp;
it shares many positive traits with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:58.260
beloved film from the Marvel Cinematic&nbsp;
universe, "Guardians of the Galaxy."

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:02.220
In the comments of the latest "Dungeons &amp;&nbsp;
Dragons: Honor Among Thieves'" trailer on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:06.360
YouTube, one person aptly subtitled the film,&nbsp;
"Guardians of the Galaxy: Fantasy Edition."

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:09.720
From the vibrant color palette to the&nbsp;
remixed Led Zeppelin backing track,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:12.780
the trailer really is packed with&nbsp;
"Guardians" vibes. This could work&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:16.140
in "Honor Among Thieves'" favor if it is&nbsp;
able to capture the magic of that film.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:19.680
"Guardians of the Galaxy" was a runaway&nbsp;
hit that turned some of comics' most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:22.860
obscure characters into household&nbsp;
names overnight. Because it couldn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:26.460
rely exclusively on name recognition,&nbsp;
"Guardians of the Galaxy's" success&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:30.060
was due largely to the sharp humor&nbsp;
and vibrant direction of James Gunn.

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:32.640
"Hey! If it isn't Star Prince."

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:34.500
"Starlord."

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:36.180
"Oh, sorry, Lord."

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:40.380
Now, the tone Gunn found in "Guardians&nbsp;
of the Galaxy" is being felt in "Honor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:43.680
Among Thieves" with its brilliant blend&nbsp;
of humor with excellent characterizations.

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:47.520
To many fans, this is a great sign that&nbsp;
the creative team understands the spirit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:51.360
of "Dungeons &amp; Dragons." It's supposed to be&nbsp;
silly and feel like you and your buddies got&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:55.140
together to play a game and joke around for&nbsp;
a little bit. As one person said on Twitter:

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:57.660
"So the new D&amp;D movie is basically 'Guardians&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:00.660
of the Galaxy' with a dungeon crawl. I&nbsp;
think that's something we can work with."

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:01.740
"Sounds lovely."

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:02.520
"Quite the opposite."

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:05.880
On the r/movies subreddit, where&nbsp;
redditors gathered to discuss the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:09.060
new trailer for "Dungeons &amp; Dragons:&nbsp;
Honor Among Thieves," one user wrote,

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:12.120
"People have been saying for 8 years&nbsp;
that 'Guardians of the Galaxy' felt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:15.660
like a tabletop RPG adventure being&nbsp;
played by actual players. I wouldn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:18.480
be surprised if the pitch for this&nbsp;
movie was just holding up a blu-ray&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:21.240
of that movie and then slapping on a&nbsp;
'Lord of the Rings' sticker or two."

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:24.900
The banter isn't the only aspect of the&nbsp;
trailer that harkens back to Peter Quill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:28.980
and his crew. A perfect example of this comes in&nbsp;
the trailer's first moments, in which Michelle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:33.240
Rodriguez's Holga the Barbarian defeats a team&nbsp;
of enemies with her hands bound. Meanwhile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:36.960
Chris Pine's Edgin the Bard attempts to&nbsp;
saw his own ropes off on some stairs.

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:40.860
"You know what? I'm thinking there are&nbsp;
probably sharper stairs somewhere else."

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:44.160
This moment not only seems like something&nbsp;
that could occur on the starship Milano,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:47.700
but it could also happen by dumb luck&nbsp;
in an actual D&amp;D game among friends.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:51.240
While the characters and their personalities&nbsp;
certainly resemble the "Guardians" crew,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:55.020
the overall feel of the film is what truly&nbsp;
seems to be getting fans excited for "Honor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:58.980
Among Thieves." If the film can capture that&nbsp;
familial friendship that can be found in both the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:03.900
"Guardians" franchise and the most magical games&nbsp;
of "Dungeons &amp; Dragons," it may be a huge success.

